		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3004&amp;p=25463#p25463"><![CDATA[
<blockquote class="uncited"><div>I was adding parts of the US.... 310 ...311.. etc... Takes forever.   The RadioID site wants money to generate a CSV...   Or I can pick through the total world .CSV and remove everything but USA.  In an effort to save people wasted time, has anyone found out if even all off USA will fit on a UV380?   If you don't mind sharing your culled DMR CSV database let me know.   RadioID = The new QRZ<br><br>-w</div></blockquote>Depends which radio you are using. The MD-9600/UV380/RT3S/RT90/DM1701 all have 16Mb memory and can store all IDs<br><br>Also...<br><br>We don't use the download from Radio ID, its not that clean.<br><br>We use this curated version<br><br><a href="https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ContactLists/ContactLists/master/Radioddity/GD77_WW.csv" class="postlink">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Conta ... D77_WW.csv</a><br><br>(Look in the DMR ID download screen)<br><br><br>Also if you want 310 - 319  jusy type 31 into the filter<br><br>this will get all ID's begining with 31<br><br>However depending on what radio your have , this won't fit in all the radios.<br><br>If you use the Download Callsign screen, then you can select what radio you and also set the text length and it will calculate whether all callsigns will fit in your radio<br><br>There are currently 97036   31* ID's but even using Voice Prompt memory as well as main memory, the GD77 only has space for 90494  callsigns (6 letters only,... No name)<br><br>So basically if thats what you want to have in your radio, then you may need to by a radio with more memory, like the ones listed above.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Sun Aug 20, 2023 11:27 am</p><hr />
]]></content>
